cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ProvenanceACH: analysis of competing hypotheses with an evidence ledger"
message: "Please cite both this software and Heuer's method."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23139763
authors:
  - family-names: Inderwildi
    given-names: Oliver
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4315-7839"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/oliverinderwildi/systems-analysis/tree/main/src/provenance-ach"
abstract: >-
  An implementation of Heuer's Analysis of Competing Hypotheses in which no item of evidence
  may enter the matrix without a provenance record, the conclusion inherits the weakest
  evidence class among the discriminating items, and the authorship of each hypothesis and
  item of evidence - source, analyst or language model - is recorded and reported.
keywords:
  - analysis of competing hypotheses
  - intelligence analysis
  - evidence ledger
  - provenance
  - systems analysis
references:
  - type: book
    title: "Psychology of Intelligence Analysis"
    authors:
      - family-names: Heuer
        given-names: "Richards J."
        name-suffix: Jr.
    publisher:
      name: "Center for the Study of Intelligence, Central Intelligence Agency"
    year: 1999
